{"entryId":"3147","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3147:1","sourceSha256":"2f21e774ad57288e05a8fb59beacb22eecd42048db39e2c650c9beef0231437e","englishSha256":"a887647c4b7e0635173027ab814215ec9111c4684a93aa4e941f452b6a31fb72","citations":[{"id":"3147:1:link-001","he":[21,89],"en":[34,222],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.2"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:2","assessment":"The checked Bavli explicitly limits the consequence to the lifetime of Rabbah bar Rav Huna. The first person ordered the job rather than personally taking down the trees.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3147:1:link-002","he":[91,149],"en":[280,291],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_41a.8"},"reference":"Menachot 41a:8","assessment":"The Menahot story reads Rava as host, Shabbat reads Rabbah. The incidents differ. Preserve the printed name and distinguish the digital parallels.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 41a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_41a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 119a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_119a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3147:1:link-003","he":[91,149],"en":[293,305],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_119a.2"},"reference":"Shabbat 119a:2","assessment":"The Menahot story reads Rava as host, Shabbat reads Rabbah. The incidents differ. Preserve the printed name and distinguish the digital parallels.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 119a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_119a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3147:1:link-004","he":[151,205],"en":[307,401],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_25a.4"},"reference":"Yevamot 25a:4","assessment":"The checked Bavli has this exact sending direction, both names and wording.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 25a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_25a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Bava Metzia limits the curse’s stated effect to Rabbah bar Rav Huna’s lifetime. Menahot spells the host Rava, while Shabbat spells the host Rabbah. Both spellings remain visible.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
